## Findings (all nonblocking)

- N1 [Medium] The orangewhite ball reads gold. Panel A averages #f6c55f (hue 41) against the brief #e8892c (hue 30), and the default yellow panel B averages #dfb649 (hue 44).
  greenyellow A is #65ee85 (hue 134, V 93) against #4f9a4a (hue 116, V 60). purplewhite A is #8e7af5 (hue 250) against #7b4a9e (hue 275). The unlit atlases show the same drift.
  The cause fits the recolour rule in docs/color-variants.md (option over default per channel, linear light; the red default has G 0.058 and B 0.042). The row of five still reads colourful, so W2 holds. The PM orange does not.
  Suggested change: pick the option values so the baked panel means land on the target hues, then re-cut 4 preset folders. | owner: maker; the PM decides
- N2 [Medium] The red kite has a rose top-right quarter (#f45769, hue 353; the others hue 3). The yellow kite has a lemon top-left quarter (#f7f460, hue 59; the others hue 43 to 45) and a thin lime line on two quarter edges.
  The cause fits the same rule (G ratio 9.3 for sailA, B ratio 1.4 for sailB). The default kite is clean. Suggested change: tune the option values with measured quarter means, or cut the red and the yellow kite from sources whose default equals the preset. | owner: maker; the PM decides
- N3 [Low] The brush paint tip is 76 px (9 by 12 px at 1024 px/m, about 1 percent of the 45 by 174 px bounding box, about 5 by 6 px at the stage scale). The brush also reads as a fat pencil in the renders. The geometry is unchanged from the first batch.
  Suggested change (optional): extend the paint wash to about 25 mm, or give the bristles a belly. | owner: maker; the PM decides
- N4 [Low] The gate cannot see a colour, a quarter, or a pose (the maker log says so). The maker look check covered the bluewhite ball, the purple brush, and the default kite only.
  Suggested change: a small PIL check per preset (mean colour of named boxes, hue tolerance) in the Phase 6 delivery step. | owner: orchestrator

## Limits

- I ran no ./forge inspect and no --fast command. I did not re-run measure/doctor.sh, measure/generate.sh, tsc, or the interphase status script.
- The brush composites (3x pair, tip at 6x, stage scale at 6x) did not attach, because the image tool stopped at the step limit. I measured the brush with PIL (N3) and looked at out/brush/render.png, render.purple.png, and the card.
- The cause named in N1 and N2 fits the numbers. I did not instrument the bake.
- Shell rules denied commands with redirection characters, so the Python checks avoid them.
- This role wrote only the 2 result files, plus scratch files and composites in /tmp/opencode/acc-g2/. The mech-check call rebuilt out/ball, out/kite, and out/brush (byte-equal except stats.json timing).

